# Volt hood and nose — 2026-10-30

The owner described the front as boat-like and asked for a hood more like the Tesla Model S. This pass shortens the projecting nose, reduces the bonnet crown, moves the lower bumper forward and keeps the light strip level around the rounded front. It preserves the tapered front width, existing cowl and wheel locations, rear, cabin, appearance and handling. The [official Model S exterior reference](https://www.tesla.com/ownersmanual/models/en_eu/GUID-6C6C3944-9674-4E81-A0E8-94D60B6D87B9.html) informed the shape; the game uses its own geometry and branding.

Review the final baked [dark side view](evidence/volt-model-s-nose-2026-10-30/dark/side-opposite-clean.png), [silver side view](evidence/volt-model-s-nose-2026-10-30/compatibility/side-opposite-clean.png) and [front-quarter view](evidence/volt-model-s-nose-2026-10-30/compatibility/front-quarter-low-clean.png). The [before side](evidence/volt-model-s-nose-2026-10-30/before/side-opposite-clean.png) and [before quarter](evidence/volt-model-s-nose-2026-10-30/before/front-quarter-low-clean.png) use the task-start model. The dark view is a synthetic dark finish, not an owner save.

Actual hood-buffer checks pass 16/16 in both procedural and prepared models, including three longitudinal profiles, cowl fit and wheel-to-nose distance. The centreline axle-to-nose span falls from 1.132 to 0.882 model units, about 22 cm at car scale. Prepared nose/light/opening checks pass 64/64, cabin fit 20/20, model integration 15/15, racing model 23/23 and actual Garage/race integration 58/58. Six of 122 supplemental seam assertions also fail on the exact task-start model: four hood/fender normal peaks and two simplified upper-front gaps. A newly introduced side gap was fixed before the final bake. The small pre-existing hood/fender sliver remains visible; the design is an interpretation rather than an exact Model S reproduction. The App test logged frame hitches.

The `electric_reference_car_nose_v1` directory contains 221 prepared meshes, all present and matching the five current source hashes. Five racing shadows, the Electric Garage template and header, Garage, catalogue, news and 49 livery pictures were regenerated. Detailed/simple visible triangles are 119,904/34,872; shadows total 3,128. Both desktop renderers produced 16 clean/worn captures, and a separate dark Compatibility capture was checked. Noninteractive engine commands used `scripts/run_no_crash_dialog.py` and isolated profiles.

Reload/reimport and owner/device appearance acceptance remain. No physical-device test, APK, live account/backend mutation or deployment was performed.
